[E0404] Error: cannot copy `f`
    ╭─[ err/106_owned_closure_moves/main.wip:14:13 ]
    │
 14 │     val g = f                       // two owners of one environment
    │             ┬
    │             ╰── `f` has type `own<(i64) => i64>`
    │
    │ Help: to transfer ownership, write `move f`
    │
    │ Note: a value that contains `own` has exactly one owner, so it is never copied
────╯
[E0401] Error: use of moved value `f`
    ╭─[ err/106_owned_closure_moves/main.wip:21:12 ]
    │
 20 │     val used = run(move f, 1)
    │                    ───┬──
    │                       ╰──── `f` moved here
 21 │     used + f(2)                     // the closure is gone
    │            ┬
    │            ╰── used here after the move
    │
    │ Note: after `move`, `f` holds no value until it is assigned again
────╯
[E0405] Error: cannot move `token`, which this closure captured
    ╭─[ err/106_owned_closure_moves/main.wip:27:26 ]
    │
 27 │         val taken = move token      // it holds the token, and keeps it
    │                          ──┬──
    │                            ╰──── captured, and kept while the closure lives
    │
    │ Help: take what is used up as a parameter of the closure
    │
    │ Note: a closure may be called again, so what it captured stays where it is
────╯
